{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And he blasphemed.</b> As its Targum renders — 'and he explicitly pronounced' — that he pronounced the explicit Name and blasphemed. It is the explicit Name that he heard from Sinai (Sifra)." "<b>And his mother's name was Shelomit daughter of Dibri.</b> Praise of Israel — that Scripture publicized her for this, to say that she alone was promiscuous." "<b>Shelomit.</b> For she would patter 'shalom to you,' 'shalom to you all' — chattering with words, greeting everyone with peace." "<b>Daughter of Dibri.</b> She was a talker, conversing with every man — therefore she came to ruin." "<b>Of the tribe of Dan.</b> This tells that the wicked person brings disgrace upon himself, disgrace upon his father, disgrace upon his tribe — corresponding to 'Oholiav son of Achisamakh, of the tribe of Dan' (Exodus 31) — praise upon him, praise upon his father, praise upon his tribe (Sifra)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:08:07.967703794Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}